  "concise_summary": "PKD develops a neurophilosophical theory of Ditheon (divine duality) grounded in hemispheric psychology, arguing that true Christianity emerges from a fusion of rational left-brain logos and right-brain compassion (Sedakah). He positions his 2-3-74 experience as a literal awakening of his latent rational hemisphere, making him a Ditheon being briefly embodying what Jesus sought to activate in Palestinian Jews. He disputes psychiatric interpretations and grounds this framework in Jungian collective unconscious and Pauline theology.",
  "key_claims": [
    "Ditheon (the true Christian) is a dual-self being: right-brain Sedakah (compassion) joined with left-brain logos (reason) in sacred syzygy.",
    "PKD's 2-3-74 was not mental illness but a rational meta-abstraction—his dormant left hemisphere awakening and recognizing Christianity's truth, which disinhibited his Ditheon state.",
    "Right-hemisphere-dominant people (shamanic, primitive, emotional) can access buried phylogenic collective wisdom when invaded by the rational function—this is what Jesus offered to the Jews.",
    "Schizophrenia is the pathological opposite: left-hemisphere dominance invaded by an irrational unconscious right hemisphere, not what PKD experienced.",
    "St. Sophia (divine wisdom) represents the rational thinking function of the collective unconscious, waiting to be born in right-brain-dominant consciousness to create the Christian superman.",
    "Christ literally confronts retributive fate in the dying creature, inserting his spotless presence to nullify karma and death, allowing the creature to achieve apotheosis while retaining individual identity."
  ],
